# Scanner CSV Ingestion & Manifest Export Rules

## 1. Input Scanner Normalization
Auto-detect scanner source by header signature and normalize to `{ scryfallId, tcgplayerProductId, setCode, collectorNumber, finish, condition, language, isAltered, isMisprint, quantity }` (map `'nonfoil'` <-> `'normal'` against `card_catalog.finishes`, and normalize full language strings such as `"English"`, `"Japanese"`, `"Chinese (Simplified)"`, `"Chinese (Traditional)"`, `"Portuguese (Brazil)"` to short ISO codes `en`, `ja`, `de`, `fr`, `it`, `es`, `pt`, `ko`, `ru`, `zhs`, `zht`, `ph` <= 16 chars):
- **ManaBox:** Read `Scryfall ID` directly. Map `Foil` (`normal`, `foil`, `etched`). Map `Condition` (`near_mint`->`NM`, `lightly_played`->`LP`, `moderately_played`->`MP`, `heavily_played`->`HP`, `damaged`->`DMG`). Map `Language`, `Altered`, and `Misprint`.
- **Delver Lens:** Read `Scryfall ID`. Normalize `Foil` boolean/string (`Foil`/`true`->`foil`, `Etched`->`etched`, empty/`false`->`normal`) and optional `Language`.
- **TCGplayer App:** Match `Product ID` against `card_catalog.tcgplayer_id` (or `tcgplayer_etched_id` when `Printing` contains `Etched`). Fallback to `(LOWER(Set Code), Card Number)`. Normalize `Language` to ISO code.
- **Dragon Shield:** Detect headers (`Folder Name, Quantity, Trade Quantity, Card Name, Set Code, Set Name, Card Number, Condition, Printing, Language, ...`). Normalize Dragon Shield set codes and collector numbers, resolve via `(LOWER(set_code), collector_number)`, map `Printing` (`Normal`->`normal`, `Foil`->`foil`, `Etched`/`Foil Etched`->`etched`), `Condition`, and `Language` (`English`->`en`, etc.).

## 2. Output Manifest Rules
- Escape CSV commas, quotes (`""`), and newlines per RFC-4180, and neutralize spreadsheet formula-injection prefixes (`=`, `+`, `-`, `@`, `\t`, `\r`, or leading spaces before `=+-@`, excluding plain negative decimals) as `"'..."`.
- **Card Conduit Export (`PILE_1_BUYLIST`):** Columns `Quantity, Name, Set Code, Collector Number, Finish, Condition, Scryfall ID`. Validate `>= 90%` of quantity has `P_buy >= 0.50` for Curated; for Sorted, enforce `100%` `P_buy >= 0.50` and split shipments exceeding `500` total cards into numbered batch CSVs (`<= 500` cards each).
- **Card Kingdom Buylist CSV (`PILE_1_BUYLIST` / `PILE_3_CREDIT_ARB`):** Columns `Card Name, Edition, Foil, Quantity`.
- **TCGplayer Staged CSV (`PILE_2_SINGLES` -> `tcgplayer_single`):** Columns `TCGplayer Id, Product Line, Set Name, Product Name, Title, Number, Rarity, Condition, TCG Market Price, TCG Direct Low, TCG Low Price With Shipping, TCG Low Price, Total Quantity, Add to Quantity, TCG Marketplace Price, My Store Reserve Quantity, My Store Price, Photo URL`.
- **Mana Pool Staged CSV (`PILE_2_SINGLES` -> `manapool_single`):** Columns `Scryfall ID, TCGplayer ID, Set Code, Collector Number, Name, Finish, Condition, Language, Quantity, Price USD`.
- **Discord/FB 85% Claim Markdown (`PILE_2_SINGLES` -> `p2p_85_pct`):** Price-tier grouped claim lines.
